WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.920
You just had the night of your life in beautiful&nbsp;
Las Vegas, Nevada. You spent hours shooting craps,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:10.960
dancing in clubs, and eating more than your&nbsp;
fill at the famous All You Can Eat Buffets.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:16.160
You’re staggering back to your hotel room, high on&nbsp;
life, in the early hours of the morning when you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:22.480
notice something strange: A long, dark tunnel just&nbsp;
off the side of the strip. You didn’t notice it on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:28.320
the way in, perhaps because you were distracted by&nbsp;
all the glitz, glamor, and hypnotic casino lights.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:32.880
You see the tunnel, and your over&nbsp;
stimulated mind feels drawn to it...

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:38.160
You stumble in and start walking. During&nbsp;
your walk, you can feel your bones cracking.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:43.440
They don’t shatter, like you’ve just&nbsp;
been hit by a train, they...shift.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:47.360
You feel the entire shape of you&nbsp;
bending into something different.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:54.320
But it doesn’t stop with your skeleton. Your&nbsp;
organs start to feel strange, and then your skin.&nbsp;

00:00:54.320 --> 00:01:00.880
In the complete darkness of the tunnel, you have&nbsp;
no idea what’s going on, so you just keep walking.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:05.280
Eventually, you find your way into a&nbsp;
lush, green forest. It’s beautiful,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:09.840
but it feels like it should be a million&nbsp;
miles away from the arid desert of Nevada.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:13.200
You were only in the tunnel&nbsp;
for a few minutes. What gives?

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.080
“Hello?” You call out. “Is anybody there?”

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:17.120
No answer.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:23.840
You explore further into this empty forest. It’s&nbsp;
trees as far as the eye can see, but no animals.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:29.120
That’s when you see something that catches your&nbsp;
eye: A puddle of crystal-clear water. But it’s not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:35.840
the puddle itself that draws your attention, it’s&nbsp;
what reflects back at you when you stare into it.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:39.840
At first, you can hardly believe it,&nbsp;
but as you move your mouth in shock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:45.120
and the reflection moves its mouth&nbsp;
too, it’s suddenly all too real.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:50.320
You’ve been turned into a fox.&nbsp;
An orange, bushy-tailed fox.&nbsp;

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:55.840
You scream, and bolt all the way back to the&nbsp;
tunnel that led you here. You sprint through,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:00.640
as you feel your entire body changing once&nbsp;
more. When you finally hit the wall of dry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:05.440
Vegas heat on the other side, you’re&nbsp;
human again. You breathe a sigh of relief,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:10.560
and stumble back to your hotel room. The next&nbsp;
day, you only vaguely remember what happened,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:15.280
and because you’re not crazy, you&nbsp;
assume it was all just a wild dream.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:23.040
What you just encountered is a Euclid Class SCP&nbsp;
known as SCP-2746 - a seemingly innocent tunnel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:27.520
near the Vegas strip which holds&nbsp;
a portal to a fantastical world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:32.400
designated by the Foundation as SCP-2746-1.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:37.280
By the time the Foundation discovered&nbsp;
and secured the SCP-2746 tunnel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:42.560
and began sending their field agents and&nbsp;
researchers on fact-finding expeditions inside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:46.960
the place was already a ghost town.&nbsp;
A forested land mass approximately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:52.960
111 kilometers in diameter, with no notable&nbsp;
signs of life. The Foundation discovered that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:58.080
this place had a strange effect on people&nbsp;
and animals who came in from our world.

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:02.800
Humans who entered assumed the forms of a random&nbsp;
animal, but retained their intelligence and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:09.680
vocal cords, creating talking animals. Animals&nbsp;
brought into 2746-1 retained their animalistic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:15.120
intelligence, but grew human-like vocal&nbsp;
chords, allowing them to repeat simple phrases.&nbsp;

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:21.680
Before the mass exodus or extinction event that&nbsp;
left 2746-1 barren, the Foundation figured out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:27.360
this place was populated by a whole civilization&nbsp;
of intelligent animals - like something out of a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:32.720
fairytale. These animals, through a mix&nbsp;
of brains and magic, were able to leave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:37.920
written records and create impressive&nbsp;
architecture, like homes and places of worship.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:42.800
Foundation researchers became fascinated&nbsp;
with how exactly this society operated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:47.840
and what could have led to its sudden downfall.&nbsp;
Thanks to a mix of advanced archeology and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:52.480
records left behind by the creatures,&nbsp;
this is what the Foundation determined:

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:57.760
The society these talking, intelligent animals&nbsp;
lived in was a kind of religious oligarchy -&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:03.920
meaning power was consolidated by the few in the&nbsp;
top social class. Society was divided into three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:09.120
segments - Crafters, Scholars, and Honorables&nbsp;
- with the Crafters being the most powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:15.120
members of society and Honorables being the least&nbsp;
powerful. The state-sponsored churches acted in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:20.880
worship of a being simply called “The Maker”,&nbsp;
who fills a similar role to the Abrahamic God.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:25.440
The Crafters, whose numbers totaled&nbsp;
13, were believed to be immortal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:32.160
and were responsible for building the majority&nbsp;
of the culture and architecture found in 2746-1.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:37.680
The Scholars acted as their wise assistants, and&nbsp;
the Honorables were a mixed class of artists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:42.000
carpenters, and artisans. It seemed that&nbsp;
this culture had a pretty good thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:47.920
going. No system of currency was ever invented,&nbsp;
and the economy operated on a barter system.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:51.280
The Foundation believes that,&nbsp;
initially, the citizens of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:57.040
world didn’t need to eat to survive, and so&nbsp;
only needed to barter for material goods.

00:04:57.040 --> 00:05:02.400
Though it’s worth noting that these conditions of&nbsp;
immortality only apply to natives of the region.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:07.680
People born on earth but assuming&nbsp;
animal forms while entering 2746-1&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:10.160
still need nutrition to survive.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:16.160
However, a great tragedy soon caused a fundamental&nbsp;
shift in the balance of life and society within&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:23.680
2746-1. The Maker decided it wanted to test&nbsp;
or punish its subjects with two major changes:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:28.480
First, humans would be forbidden&nbsp;
from entering the domain. And second,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:34.160
The Maker now made the consumption of food&nbsp;
necessary for continued survival and sanity.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:36.160
Nothing was ever the same.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:40.640
Because nobody had needed to eat prior&nbsp;
to this, food stores had never been made,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:46.320
and the inhabitants had no agricultural knowledge&nbsp;
that would allow them to easily mass-produce more.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:51.600
As a result, while the Crafters and Scholars were&nbsp;
able to feed on fruits from luxurious private&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:59.760
gardens, the Honorables were forced to resort to&nbsp;
eating each other, or other inhabitants of 2746-1.

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:05.520
This began a bloody rift that split society&nbsp;
from the top down. One half, led by the powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:11.280
Crafters Sari and Suwaird, wanted to preserve&nbsp;
society as it was and continue to worship The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:17.280
Maker. Sari took the form of a Flemish giant&nbsp;
rabbit, and Suwaird appeared as a house cat.

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:22.080
The opposition, led by Former Crafters&nbsp;
Fredrick and Agathos - with the reluctant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:27.440
help of a scholar named Clovis - wanted to&nbsp;
get revenge on The Maker for all he’d done,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:33.360
and kill him, completely altering society.
Don’t be fooled by their appearances though.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:38.640
Many of the inhabitants of 2746-1&nbsp;
wree fiercely intelligent sorcerers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:44.800
and the apocalyptic civil war they sparked came&nbsp;
to be known to the Foundation as Event Nachash.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:47.840
Like many wars, there would be no real winners&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:52.320
here - only survivors. And&nbsp;
even then, not for long.

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:57.280
It was a bloody and horrific war. All&nbsp;
attempts at finding a diplomatic solution&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:03.360
failed. Fredrick and Agathos would not stop&nbsp;
until they had The Maker’s blood on their paws.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:08.400
In the end, though, they were defeated,&nbsp;
and for their traitorous crimes they were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:13.360
to be punished by Sari and Suwaird in&nbsp;
horrific ways to make examples of them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:18.320
Since neither could die, they were&nbsp;
given fates worse than death instead.

00:07:18.320 --> 00:07:24.160
Fredrick was up first. Before the war, he’d been&nbsp;
a leader prized for his courage and ingenuity.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:29.440
He’d created something known as the “great fire”,&nbsp;
which had provided the kingdom with light. For his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:34.960
so-called “Atrocities against the maker”, he was&nbsp;
given the punishment of “permanent crucifixion”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:40.480
and relocation to a place known as the “under&nbsp;
plane.” His snout was cut off his face,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:45.920
and he was set permanently ablaze, in a manner&nbsp;
that would leave him forever suffering, and would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:52.560
make him appear to look like a monster to all.
Next went Agathos. She was Fredrick’s sister,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:57.200
and was seen as the mastermind of many&nbsp;
of their schemes. She would be forever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:02.640
encased in white clay, and bled through&nbsp;
her eyes until the sin drains from her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:08.560
She’s now a living, crying statue, existing in a&nbsp;
state of permanent imprisonment for her part in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:13.760
the crimes against The Maker. Clovis, because&nbsp;
her involvement in the coup was unwilling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:18.720
was given a more minor punishment - One of&nbsp;
her eyes was removed, and she was permanently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:26.160
placed in a broken human body, effectively&nbsp;
banishing her from her home in 2746 - 1 forever.&nbsp;

00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:31.840
Though they may have won, things didn’t end much&nbsp;
better for Sari and Suwaird. The civil war had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:37.600
fractured their world, and in the aftermath, the&nbsp;
survivors chose to leave in hopes of finding a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:43.040
better life elsewhere. Sari and Suwaird though,&nbsp;
felt partly responsible for everything that had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:49.200
happened, and so they decided to remain in their&nbsp;
dying world. Before they themselves died - or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:55.760
perhaps moved on to different forms, leaving their&nbsp;
animal bodies behind - they left a final note.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.760 --> 00:09:01.840
It was from this note that the Foundation&nbsp;
learned much of the story of SCP-2746.

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:07.760
This may seem like a pretty open and shut case.&nbsp;
Another magical realm destroyed by tragedy and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:14.800
civil war, much like the land of Fantasy in&nbsp;
SCP-1762. But what’s really bizarre here is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:20.320
that this is only the tip of the iceberg when it&nbsp;
comes to the stories of some of these key figures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:25.920
in the Event Nachash. First, what became&nbsp;
of the two rebels, Agathos and Fredrick?

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:32.960
Today, they’re two parts of the feared and&nbsp;
deadly SCP-1913. Fredrick, now going by Freddie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:38.240
is a nightmarish, faceless fire-demon in&nbsp;
the form of a dog, slavishly devoted to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:44.880
the protection of his sister - Agathos, now&nbsp;
known as Agatha. Still trapped in white clay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:49.760
her leaking blood now deadly to the touch.
Clovis is still believed to be in league&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.760 --> 00:09:56.720
with Agathos and Fredrick, and may now be&nbsp;
related to the sinister SCP-1903 - a one-eyed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.720 --> 00:10:02.720
rabbit-like human.But strangest of all is the&nbsp;
possible truth behind Sari and Suwaird, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:11.040
two devotees to The Maker who remained in 2746-1&nbsp;
until their very last breath. In all likelihood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:16.640
these two were once agents of the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation‘s infamous Las Vegas branch.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:20.160
They took on these more animalistic&nbsp;
forms after their deaths.

00:10:20.160 --> 00:10:25.440
Sari may have once been Agent Sarah Crowley,&nbsp;
a Japanese-American woman who died in the line&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:31.600
of duty in 1960. Suwaird was once Dr.&nbsp;
Stuart Hayward, Crowley’s partner - his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:36.720
new name acting as a kind of fusion of&nbsp;
the first and last name he had in life.

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:41.680
This is only the beginning of the animal-themed&nbsp;
weirdness occurring around Site 45,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:46.320
the Foundation’s Vegas branch, but this&nbsp;
series of anomalies - collected under&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:50.160
the term “Pitch Haven” - will&nbsp;
have to wait for another video.

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:56.160
After all, you know what they say:&nbsp;
What happens in Vegas, stays in Vegas.

00:10:56.160 --> 00:11:02.640
Now check out “SCP-001 - The Scarlet&nbsp;
King” and “SCP-2317 - The Devourer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:08.960
Of Worlds / A Door To Another World” for more&nbsp;
mind-blowing accounts from the SCP Foundation.

